# fleet_capacity.txtar
#
# Documents the `cascade fleet capacity [--json]` behavioral scenarios
# this ticket's contract names (P1-E31-W6-S63-T4). This module carries no
# testscript (rogpeppe/testscript) dependency -- see the sibling
# fleet-sessions.txtar / context-slice.txtar / context-scope-show.txtar,
# which make the identical call: adding one needs a license gate this
# repo has not cleared. The scenarios below are instead expressed as
# executable Go in cmd/cascade/fleet_capacity_test.go: mount reachability
# and the mutation proof (TestFleetCapacityMountedOnRoot), the no-daemon
# actionable refusal (TestFleetCapacity_NoDaemon_ActionableError), a
# positional argument refusal (TestFleetCapacity_ExtraArgRefused), human
# table rendering for both a populated and an empty snapshot
# (TestFleetCapacitySnapshot_TableHasRequiredColumns,
# TestFleetCapacitySnapshot_EmptyTableHasHeaderOnly), the --json envelope
# shape (TestFleetCapacityResult_JSONEnvelope,
# TestFleetCapacityResult_EmptyJSONEnvelope), and CASCADE_NO_INPUT parity
# (TestFleetCapacity_CASCADE_NO_INPUT_Identical). This file records the
# intended script form for when a testscript dependency is cleared.

# One-shot human output on an isolated environment (no daemon reachable)
# is refused with an actionable message, not a panic or a fabricated
# empty snapshot -- a FleetSnapshot is the daemon's own in-memory state
# (S-63.T1's Compositor), never something this command reconstructs
# standalone.
! exec cascade fleet capacity
stderr 'cascade daemon run'

# --json emits the versioned envelope (the SAME repo-wide contract every
# other cascade --json command uses; see fleet_capacity.go's header,
# deviation 2) -- automation parity, no interactive prompts either way.
! exec cascade --json fleet capacity
stdout '"ok":\s*false'

# A positional argument is refused.
! exec cascade fleet capacity extra-arg
stderr 'unknown command'

# CASCADE_NO_INPUT=1 produces the identical refusal -- this command never
# branches on interactivity.
env CASCADE_NO_INPUT=1
! exec cascade fleet capacity
stderr 'cascade daemon run'
